course: dictionary
lesson: 1708
title: Cinchona: a tree that gave us medicine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cinchona is a tree or shrub from the Andes mountains of South America. Its bark contains a substance called quinine.
explain: Cinchona bark is the dried bark of this tree. For centuries, people used it to treat malaria, a serious illness spread by mosquito bites. «Knowledge flowed both ways: Andean peoples knew that cinchona bark helped with fever» shows that people in the Andes knew about its healing power long before Europe did.
explain: Use context to find the meaning. In «Quinine, from the bark of the cinchona tree, was known to Andean peoples», the words «from the bark of the cinchona tree» tell you where quinine comes from. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A cinchona is a tree or shrub from the Andes mountains of South America.
fact: Cinchona bark is the dried bark of this tree.
fact: Quinine is found in cinchona bark and was the first effective medicine against malaria.
fact: Quinine gives tonic water its bitter taste.
fact: The cinchona tree appears on Peru's coat of arms.
exercise: «Quinine, from the bark of the cinchona tree, was known to Andean peoples.» Where does quinine come from? | *The bark of the cinchona tree | Mountain rocks | Maize seeds | Potatoes
exercise: What was cinchona bark used to treat for centuries? | Sunburn | Broken arms | *Malaria | Fever and malaria
exercise: Where do cinchona trees grow? | The Scottish Highlands | *The Andes mountains of South America | Coasts of Australia | Deserts in Africa
test: What gives tonic water its bitter taste? | Salt | *Quinine from cinchona bark | Sugar | Lemon juice
test: «Quinine ... became the main medicine for malaria for centuries.» What does the word centuries suggest? | A single week | Hundreds of years | *A very long time, hundreds of years | Just one season
exam: What does the word cinchona mean? | *A tree or shrub from the Andes whose bark contains quinine | A medicine you buy in a chemist's shop | A fizzy drink with lemon | A mountain in Peru
